  "cause": {
    "proximate_text": "due to flexure in the breaker cell switch mounting support the cell switch experienced enough displacement as the bypass breaker was racked into position to cause the switch to remain closed... the direct cause of the turbine trip signal was a design characteristic of the cubicle design that allowed for the flexing of the cell switch support structure, which resulted in the failure of the switch to change state",
